The Node local-process adapter uses a small executable built from the adjacent
local-process-launcher.c (the repository's Apache-2.0 license). It performs only
POSIX resource-limit, fork/watchdog and exec operations; it is not a language
interpreter or an execution policy.

Darwin executables dynamically use the operating system's libSystem; no Apple
runtime library is bundled. Linux executables are built with Alpine GCC 14.2.0
and statically link musl 1.2.5. The included musl COPYRIGHT is from the upstream
1.2.5 source release. GCC runtime terms are included for compiler runtime parts:
COPYING3 plus the GCC Runtime Library Exception (COPYING.RUNTIME).

Upstream license sources:
https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.5.tar.gz (COPYRIGHT)
https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/blob/releases/gcc-14.2.0/COPYING3
https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/blob/releases/gcc-14.2.0/COPYING.RUNTIME

Compiler identification, base-image digest and each executable's SHA-256 are
recorded in local-process-manifest.json. Rebuilds are a maintainer operation;
installation and execution never invoke a compiler, package manager or Python.
